Scope and explicit changes from the upstream Xlib Makefile:
  80 unchanged engine translation-unit selections + doom-headless.c in place
  of doomgeneric_xlib.c. Resolution 320x200; virtual clock and no live keyboard.
  Source changes are limited to the separately hashed doom-video-init.patch.
  All other unpacked source/header/Makefile bytes are checked against the pin.
  GNU11/O2 instead of upstream Os; no ggdb3/Wall; no X11 or sound dependency.
  -fwrapv supplied to ALL THREE compilers, not just EvoCC.
  Target libc/libm/CRT and assembler/linker remain reference infrastructure.
  Every subject object, including the platform adapter, is EvoCC-generated.
  Subject objects cannot fall back: failed emission stops before native link.

Preserved negative attempts in .build/ladder/doom:
  attempt-1-unsupported-wall.json: EvoCC explicitly refuses -Wall.
  attempt-2-first-trap.json / attempt-2-runtime.json / attempt-2/:
    all 81 units compile and link, but EvoCC traps before frame 1 (E3004).
    Diagnostic-only signal trace maps PC 0x43bbcc to P_SpawnMapThing.
    The ANG45 * (mthing->angle/45) expression performs signed multiplication
    before assignment to angle_t. doom-angle-wrap.c reduces it to angle 270:
    6 * 536870912 exceeds INT_MAX. GCC14 and Clang19 UBSan both diagnose it;
    EvoCC C-HIR/EvoIR report E3004 without wrapping and return 0 with -fwrapv.
    The final regression also checks MIR at O0/O2. No guard is suppressed.
  attempt-3/:
    with wrapping, all compilers execute both demos successfully, but the first
    27 frames vary even across GCC self-repeats. Later frames agree.
    i_video.c allocates I_VideoBuffer using Z_Malloc without initializing it;
    the first D_Display wipe captures that old screen. The explicit one-line
    memset repair gives the initial prior screen defined bytes for every build.
    Final acceptance includes every frame, including the initial melt.
  attempt-4-sanitizer-contract.json / attempt-4-summary.json:
    the auxiliary test incorrectly expected Clang's explicit signed-overflow
    sanitizer not to diagnose -fwrapv. The positive now executes the ordinary
    wrapping program; both unwrapped negatives remain sanitized. The sealed
    image lacks Clang's optional sanitizer archive, so its instrumented object
    uses the compatible GCC libubsan runtime. This is disclosed, not a skipped
    oracle. The first common-entry attempt also lacked driverSha256 at the
    required receipt location and was correctly rejected as ERROR.

Acceptance:
  81/81 EvoCC translation units assembled, complete subject link, no fallback.
  GCC14/Clang19 separately compile all the same 81 C units and link.
  demo1/demo2 x two repeats x three compilers = 12 normal exit-0 executions.
  Each streams exactly 350 complete 320x200x4 frames; 4,200 frame instances.
  Corresponding full SHA-256 sequences agree across compilers and repetitions.
  Each demo has over 100 distinct frames; a repeated black frame cannot pass.
  No warm-up frame is dropped. Runtime binary/object hashes survive unchanged.
  A few rendered PPM snapshots are retained; full raw video is streamed, not
  stored. Native execution is offline, within the existing ARM64 container.
  Reference tools/libc, source/compiler/adapter/image identities are captured.

